# Portable 2D sprite and animation specializations

## Objective

Provide two bounded skills and two agent briefs for 2D sprite consistency and animation review, prioritizing the user's Godot + ChatGPT workflow. Their deliverables distinguish image consistency, temporal continuity, engine integration and human acceptance.

## Context and evidence

Draft revision 2 incorporates the user's 2026-10-07 prerequisite requirement. [Revision notes](revision-notes.md) preserve the earlier proposal's scope and the reason for this refinement. No approved plan is replaced.

- [User request and discovery](../../evidence/SPEC-003-game-dev-specializations/discovery.md).
- [Reviewable recommendation](../../vault/drafts/game-dev-specializations-2026-10-07.md).
- [Primary sources](../../vault/research/game-animation-sources-2026-10-07.md).
- [Approved game path](../../vault/canon/DEC-001-game-guidance.md).
- Existing game templates and optional plugin skills can be reused. No real game/asset has been supplied or diagnosed.
- [SPEC-004](../SPEC-004-add-readiness-and-progress/spec.md) defines the common visual readiness/progress/status contract proposed before these packages.

## Scope

- Portable `atena-game-sprite-fit` and `atena-game-sprite-animation-review` skill packages under `templates/automation/game/skills/`, each with one focused reference.
- Technical artist and game QA briefs under `templates/automation/game/agents/`, with deliverable, read/write scope, handoff and limits.
- Two optional templates: `templates/game/sprite-contract.md` and `templates/game/sprite-motion-review.md`, covering applicable 2D fields and Godot integration without mandating pixel art or cutout animation.
- Links and minimal routing guidance in GAMES.md and templates/AGENTS.md.
- Validation of skill structure, references, role boundaries, contract and realistic documentary scenarios.
- Both skills/briefs check applicable visual bible, character identity, position/presentation and scene context before visual work; missing readiness returns control to Atena's discovery rather than initiating production/review.

## Non-goals

- Repair/generate/download assets, create a game scene or claim runtime/motion quality validation.
- Choose/change the engine, buy tools, install dependencies, invoke providers, configure credentials or spend credits.
- Install skills globally or activate agents automatically; delegate live work without a bounded authorization.
- Implement SPEC-002 or create a new workspace/schema/framework.
- Add 3D rigging/retargeting guidance in this first implementation.
- Modify DEC-001, existing approval semantics or lore; publish, push or merge.

## Decisions

| Decision | Proposed choice | Rationale | Status |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Priority | 2D consistency and animation diagnosis first | User confirmed sprites, Godot + ChatGPT | confirmed requirement |
| Packaging | Portable repository packages, optional project adoption later | ADD is portable; avoid changing user-global behavior | proposed default |
| Breadth | Sprites first, with frame-by-frame and cutout decision criteria | Style unspecified; avoid imposing a technique | proposed default |
| Roles | Technical artist owns bounded candidate; QA owns bounded evidence | Named deliverables and clear integration owner | proposed |
| Tools | Reuse relevant image generation/editing and visual debugging; record missing capability | Avoid duplicate implementations or mandatory plugins | proposed |
| Readiness | Require the common bible/identity/position/scene contract before acting | User's new explicit requirement, SPEC-004 | confirmed requirement |
| Integration owner | Atena integrates findings into the milestone spec | Prevent conflicting edits and acceptance claims | proposed |

## Gaps

### BLOCKING

- SPEC-004's common readiness contract must be approved and implemented before this package plan is executable. This draft remains unapproved and is not presented as execution-ready.
- Approval mode and checkpoint are pending authorization requirements, not granted authority.
- Real asset, project/engine version and reproducible symptoms are required for a later repair pilot; that pilot is excluded here.

### RESOLVABLE

- Storage: repository-portable templates, no global installation.
- Examples: 2D proportion/pivot drift, timing/contact defects and Godot playback/configuration; pixel-art/cutout remain conditional techniques.
- Thresholds: chosen per project/camera/reference rather than universal numeric values.
- Validation: structural and documentary scenarios; actual runtime evidence stays pending until a separately authorized pilot.

### DEFERRED

- Live pilot, engine-specific adapters, deterministic inspection scripts, generated assets and automatic repairs.
- Design, gameplay, level, audio, UI, performance and delivery specializations beyond this first scope.
- 3D rigs and retargeting.
- SPEC-002 implementation and publication.

## Acceptance criteria

See [acceptance.md](acceptance.md). Criteria cover meaningful triggers, image/sequence/engine diagnostics, sprite conventions, distinct agent boundaries, traceable handoffs, truthful evidence and structural validation.

## Impact

### Expected files/systems

Ten official files: two skill entrypoints, two references, two agent briefs, two game templates, GAMES.md and templates/AGENTS.md. Run records and plan state only within an approved execution. Existing templates remain usable independently.

### Canonical impact

No canonical record promotion or revision proposed. Adoption adds optional operational guidance consistent with DEC-001. Approval of this exact scope authorizes the specified templates and routing additions, not a material revision of a game's intent.

## Plan of flight and validation

See [PLAN-003](plan.md). Review realistic scenarios without claiming a real engine run or independent assessment. Verify packages with the skill-creator validator where available and validate links/IDs/state. A future pilot measures practical value before global installation or expansion.

## Evidence and reconciliation

Preparation in [discovery.md](../../evidence/SPEC-003-game-dev-specializations/discovery.md). Authorized implementation must record actual outputs, criteria, limitations and remaining pilot work before clearing the cursor. SPEC-002 stays draft and separate.

## Risks

- Excess roles/paperwork: two skills and two briefs; invoke only for a bounded need.
- Superficial animation fixes: require hypotheses and image/sequence/engine comparison; visual acceptance cannot be inferred from import success.
- Style overgeneralization: preserve pixel-art/illustration distinctions and evaluate intentional pose deformation separately from identity drift.
- Tool dependency: optional routing with missing-capability reporting and no silent installation.
- Fictional tests mistaken for evidence: explicit illustrative labels and pending runtime status.

## Post-hoc disclosure

Not applicable. Only inspection, research and proposal preparation preceded approval; no skill packages or official process changes have been implemented.
